n2x|n|An elongated fish of many genera and species. The common eels of Europe and America belong to the genus Anguilla. The electrical eel is a species of Gymnotus. The so called vinegar eel is a minute nematode worm. See Conger eel, Electric eel, and Gymnotus.	a:nd5,91,6;pq6,76,2;2l9,71,2~nd5,91,6;pq6,76,2;2l9,71,2	n:1avs,185,5;1mtn,156,7;nd5,66,1~1mtn,156,7;1avs,185,5;nd5,66,1	N:zk1,160,7~zk1,160,7
